# Projects layout baseline (saved preference)

User liked this layout as of Aug 2026. Restore to it if experiments don't land.

## Structure
- Typographic case studies — **no product screenshots**
- Each card: **large number top-left**, **logo/monogram top-right** (same for featured + secondary)
- Then: title, one-line description, middot tags (prefer just `Full-stack`)
- OpenOnion: archived with stamp — **chosen: E footer + B worn dashed ring**
- Grid: featured Lawpath full-width first, then OpenOnion | Vocal AI in two columns with vertical hairline between

## Logos
- Lawpath: `/lawpath-logo.png` with `logoTone="mono"`
- OpenOnion: `/openonionlogo.svg` + `/openonionlogo-dark.svg` via `logoDark`
- Vocal AI: `monogram="VA"` until a real mark exists
- Logo size preference: ~`h-12 sm:h-14`, max-width ~`11rem`

## Chosen stamp: `stampVariant="footer"`
- Straight (no rotation), sits under the Full-stack tag
- Visual style from B: solid border + worn dashed outer ring (`::after`)
- Text: **Company pivoted**
- Does not overlay/fade the description

## Do not regress to
- Platform screenshots as project visuals
- Lawpath logo nested under “Feature” in the text column
- Mono filter on OpenOnion SVG
- Solid opaque black stamp that blocks description
